{
  "_comment": "Golden slice of the CORRECTED OpenAPI document (openapi-numeric-schema-truth). After the IOpenApiSchemaTransformer strips the spurious .NET 10 string arm, every numeric body/response field declares a SINGLE JSON type ('integer' or 'number'), never the ['integer','string']/['number','string'] union. Representative schemas below cover int32, int64, double, nullable numerics, arrays, and $ref reuse. Child specs cite field name + single type VERBATIM from here (verbatim-fixture-citation rule). Timestamps/EntityId stay 'string' as before (not part of the numeric union).",
